ent-citations><nplcit status="new"><text>See also references of EP     1018490A1</text><sources><source name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources> </nplcit> <nplcit status="new"><text>TAKAO JOUBU, "Jiko Kaiseki No Jissai Glass Hahen No Yasashii Shirabekata", METALS, (1998), Vol. 68, No. 11, pages 1025-1028, XP002926131.</text> <sources><source category="X" name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></nplcit></non-patent-citations></citations></technical-data><parties><applicants><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>KIKUTA MASASHI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>MAENAKA MASAYUKI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>NIPPON SHEET GLASS CO LTD</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>SAKAI CHIHIRO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KIKUTA, MASASHI</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>MAENAKA, MASAYUKI</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>NIPPON SHEET GLASS CO., LTD.</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SAKAI, CHIHIRO</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>KIKUTA MASASHI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>MAENAKA MASAYUKI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>SAKAI CHIHIRO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KIKUTA, MASASHI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>MAENAKA, MASAYUKI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SAKAI, CHIHIRO</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>In a production process for air-quench toughened glass plates, a failed glass plate containing nickel sulfide (NiS) is removed through subjecting it to an effective forced fracture. Such forced fracture is carried out during batchwise soaking treatment after a toughening step, or in a toughening step after causing cracks to occur in an annealing step before the toughening step, or in a toughening step after causing cracks to occur in a pretreatment step before the toughening step, or during continuous annealing after a toughening step. This method can be used for producing a high quality toughened glass plate free of NiS.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>Dans un procédé permettant de produire des plaques de verre trempé refroidi à l'air, on élimine une plaque de verre défectueuse, contenant du sulfure de nickel (NiS), en la soumettant à une véritable fracture forcée. On réalise cette fracture forcée soit durant le traitement de cuisson par lots suivant une étape de trempe, soit durant une étape de trempe faisant suite à la survenue de fissures durant une étape de recuisson précédant ladite étape de trempe, soit durant une étape de trempe faisant suite à la survenue de fissures durant une étape de prétraitement précédent ladite étape de trempe, soit durant la recuisson continue suivant une étape de trempe. Ce procédé peut être utilisé pour produire une plaque de verre trempé de haute qualité exempt de NiS.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>